From: Aaron N <aaronna@valvesoftware.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: no firmware log stream without tracing, u64
 BSS flag cache

Two Steam Frame kernel fixes, carried as one:

1. Don't ask the firmware for its log stream unless it can be
   consumed. ath12k_qmi_wlanfw_wlan_ini_send() always set enable_fwlog,
   so the firmware sends DIAG events, up to hundreds per second, that
   ath12k_wmi_diag_event() only hands to a tracepoint. Without
   CONFIG_ATH12K_TRACING each one is received and dropped.
   enable_fwlog now follows CONFIG_ATH12K_TRACING.
2. Keep the cached BSS change mask as u64. mac80211 passes
   link_info_changed() a u64 mask, and ath12k caches it for links whose
   vdev does not exist yet, to replay once the vdev is assigned. A u32
   cache truncated flags above bit 31, such as BSS_CHANGED_TPE.

Squashed from the Steam Frame kernel's sm8650-7.2 branch, bodies
identical:
  4ed1ce3fa ath12k: don't send DIAG events if there is no sink
  a498f595a wifi: ath12k: use u64 for cached BSS change flags
A third, 9f9eb662a (complete regd_update_completed on dropped reg
events), is in 7.3.6 as 4e566abff512.
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.h | 2 +-
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/qmi.c  | 2 +-
 2 files changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.h b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.h
index b8fc06825..d68b08556 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.h
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.h
@@ -292,7 +292,7 @@ struct ath12k_key_conf {
 struct ath12k_vif_cache {
 	struct ath12k_tx_conf tx_conf;
 	struct ath12k_key_conf key_conf;
-	u32 bss_conf_changed;
+	u64 bss_conf_changed;
 };
 
 struct ath12k_rekey_data {
diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/qmi.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/qmi.c
index 8c7c1936f..7b1c46698 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/qmi.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/qmi.c
@@ -3777,7 +3777,7 @@ static int ath12k_qmi_wlanfw_wlan_ini_send(struct ath12k_base *ab)
 	int ret;
 
 	req.enable_fwlog_valid = true;
-	req.enable_fwlog = 1;
+	req.enable_fwlog = IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_ATH12K_TRACING) ? 1 : 0;
 
 	ret = qmi_txn_init(&ab->qmi.handle, &txn,
 			   qmi_wlanfw_wlan_ini_resp_msg_v01_ei, &resp);
